<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  §9.1 usage descriptions.

  Every string below says *what is read*, *what it is used for*, and — where
  it is the user's likely worry — *what is not read*. §9.1 is explicit that
  vague descriptions get rejected ("泛泛而谈会被拒"), and the specific thing
  reviewers look for is whether the stated purpose matches the data breadth
  the app actually requests.

  Note what is absent: `NSHealthShareUsageDescription`. HealthKit is Phase 3
  (§10, and R4 ranks it last precisely because it carries the most review
  friction). Shipping a usage description for a capability the app does not
  request reads as scope the app has not justified, so the string is kept in
  `../README.md` ready to paste in when the entitlement is added rather than
  sitting here unused.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>CFBundleDevelopmentRegion</key>
  <string>zh_CN</string>
  <key>CFBundleDisplayName</key>
  <string>PAgent</string>
  <key>CFBundleExecutable</key>
  <string>$(EXECUTABLE_NAME)</string>
  <key>CFBundleIdentifier</key>
  <string>$(PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER)</string>
  <key>CFBundleInfoDictionaryVersion</key>
  <string>6.0</string>
  <key>CFBundleName</key>
  <string>$(PRODUCT_NAME)</string>
  <key>CFBundlePackageType</key>
  <string>APPL</string>
  <key>CFBundleShortVersionString</key>
  <string>$(MARKETING_VERSION)</string>
  <key>CFBundleVersion</key>
  <string>$(CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION)</string>
  <key>LSRequiresIPhoneOS</key>
  <true/>
  <key>UILaunchScreen</key>
  <dict/>
  <key>UISupportedInterfaceOrientations</key>
  <array>
    <string>UIInterfaceOrientationPortrait</string>
  </array>

  <!-- Calendars and Reminders. The iOS 17+ full-access keys; the older
       NSCalendarsUsageDescription is not read on this deployment target. -->
  <key>NSCalendarsFullAccessUsageDescription</key>
  <string>PAgent 读取你的日程来找出空闲时段，并在你逐项确认后把安排好的行程写回日历。未经你点击确认，PAgent 不会创建或修改任何日程。</string>
  <key>NSRemindersFullAccessUsageDescription</key>
  <string>PAgent 在你确认行程后，为需要准备的事项创建提醒。未经你确认不会写入任何提醒。</string>

  <!-- Location. Both keys are present because §9.3 requires the staged
       request: ask for WhenInUse first, and only offer the upgrade once the
       user has seen the feature work. The upgrade prompt needs the Always
       key already declared. -->
  <key>NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
  <string>PAgent 用你当前的位置推荐附近的去处，并估算行程之间的通勤时间。</string>
  <key>NSLocationAlwaysAndWhenInUseUsageDescription</key>
  <string>PAgent 在后台识别你常去的区域（例如「常在城西活动」），据此推荐更顺路的去处。它只在你到访和离开时记录区域，不做持续定位；你也可以只允许「使用时」访问，推荐依然可用。</string>

  <!-- Photos. The "metadata only" clause is the load-bearing part: §4.1 reads
       `PHAsset.location` and `creationDate` and never touches pixels, which is
       both the privacy posture and the thing a reviewer will want stated. -->
  <key>NSPhotoLibraryUsageDescription</key>
  <string>PAgent 只读取照片的拍摄时间与拍摄地点，用来了解你去过哪些地方。它不读取、不分析、也不上传照片内容本身。</string>

  <!-- §9.3 "AI 功能披露": the user is told at first launch and in settings
       that complex planning sends the profile card to Anthropic. This string
       is the copy the onboarding screen uses, kept here so it is reviewed
       alongside the permission strings it belongs with. -->
  <key>PAgentCloudProcessingDisclosure</key>
  <string>复杂行程规划会把一张不超过 500 token 的「画像卡」发送至 Anthropic 处理。画像卡的完整原文可以在「设置 → 我发出去了什么」中随时查看。你的日历、位置、照片等原始数据不会离开这台设备。</string>

  <!-- The proxy origin. Deliberately empty rather than defaulted: a
       placeholder URL would turn "forgot to configure this" into a confusing
       network error at the first request instead of a clear message at
       launch. Set per-configuration so a TestFlight build can point at a
       staging proxy without a code change. -->
  <key>PAgentProxyBaseURL</key>
  <string></string>

  <key>BGTaskSchedulerPermittedIdentifiers</key>
  <array>
    <!-- §6.1's nightly digest. Runs on `BGProcessingTask` so it only fires
         while charging and idle — on-device inference is expensive enough
         that running it opportunistically would show up as battery drain. -->
    <string>com.example.PAgent.nightly-digest</string>
  </array>

  <key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
  <array>
    <string>processing</string>
  </array>

  <key>NSAppTransportSecurity</key>
  <dict>
    <!-- No exceptions. The only host the app talks to is our own proxy over
         HTTPS; an ATS exception here would be the easiest way to accidentally
         weaken the one network path that carries the profile card. -->
    <key>NSAllowsArbitraryLoads</key>
    <false/>
  </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
